{"name":"Skydome","hex":"#38a3cc","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"skydome","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sphere or hemisphere with a texture on its inner face, used to simulate the sky or similar backdrop around a three-dimensional playfield."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skydome"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rogers Centre","blocks":[{"text":"Rogers Centre is a retractable roof stadium in downtown Toronto, Ontario, Canada, situated at the base of the CN Tower near the northern shore of Lake Ontario. Opened in 1989 on the former Railway Lands, it is home to the Toronto Blue Jays of Major League Baseball (MLB). As well as being improved over the decades, during the MLB offseasons of 2022–24, the stadium was renovated by upgrading the sports facilities and hospitality whilst reducing the capacity for baseball games. While it is primarily a sports venue, the stadium also hosts other large events such as conventions, trade fairs, concerts, travelling carnivals, circuses and monster truck shows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Rogers_Centre_%28500_Level%29_-_Toronto%2C_ON.jpg/330px-Rogers_Centre_%28500_Level%29_-_Toronto%2C_ON.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rogers_Centre","wikidata":"Q76318"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Suspension_bridge_over_railway_tracks_SkyDomeRogersCentre.JPG/500px-Suspension_bridge_over_railway_tracks_SkyDomeRogersCentre.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Suspension_bridge_over_railway_tracks_SkyDomeRogersCentre.JPG/1280px-Suspension_bridge_over_railway_tracks_SkyDomeRogersCentre.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Suspension_b